Z||000007||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||01-27-2001||09:37 PM||||Ferris Beuler's Day Off - <P>There is a 1986 SE V6 white automatic Fiero with the tan interior in at least three scenes.  The car is a plot point in the relationship between Ferris and his Sister Jeanie.  Jeanie got a Fiero and Ferris got a computer.  The movie was made in 1986 and the Fiero looks like it just rolled off the showroom floor.  There are also lots of scenes with a Ferrari (actually a 280z kit car) that eventually gets killed in the end.<P>I am sure everyone has seen this movie.  It was the reason I choose the 2m4 style Fiero in white with a tan interior.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||01-27-2001||09:42 PM||||It's not an '86SE. It is a STDI bumper pad Fiero. Since it has speaker seat headrests, it has to be an '84-'85, I always assumed it was an '85. Also, to be an '86 SE it would need aero front fascia, ground effects, and black skirt accents. The car in the movie has none.||||reg||1
